+# Host integration tests
+
+Build with an installed crypto backend, for example
+`make HAVE_WOLFSSL=1 STRIP=true`. Run `make test` for native unit tests and
+`make test-cgi HAVE_WOLFSSL=1` for real CGI requests on the loopback interface.
+CGI tests use a synchronous JSON helper fixture and exercise live encoder
+settings, supported options, persistence, imaging transactions and faults.
+
+Schema checks require Python packages `lxml` and `xmlschema` (tested with
+6.1.3 and 4.3.2). Fetch the official definitions once:
+
+```
+python3 test/fetch_schemas.py /tmp/onvif-schemas
+ONVIF_SCHEMA_DIR=/tmp/onvif-schemas python3 test/test_schema.py
+```
+
+ONVIF files are pinned to `68ee1b540a40f848c9599eba2c55b87547c588d6`
+of `onvif/specs`. External W3C/OASIS dependencies retain their published
+locations; the downloaded manifest records their SHA-256 hashes. Definitions
+remain unchanged. Validation runs offline using XSD 1.1 because recent ONVIF
+content models contain optional elements followed by `##any` wildcards.
+The tests validate complete service responses for JPEG, H264, H265, source
+configuration, URI, capabilities and helper-backed encoder/imaging reads.
+
+HTTP checks require a host-runnable uhttpd executable. Supply its command as
+a JSON argument array, including any loader arguments needed on the host:
+
+```
+UHTTPD_COMMAND='["/usr/sbin/uhttpd"]' python3 test/test_http.py
+```
+
+The test starts an isolated server on a temporary loopback port, installs
+CGI wrappers and checks profile enumeration and SOAP HTTP fault status.
+No camera or RTSP server is required by these protocol tests.
